world2vec-toy demo — NOTICE

This directory (apps/world2vec-toy/) is a CPU-only clear-experiment
toy inspired by:

  Schmidt, Gonzalez Laiz, Szuppinger, Schneider,
  "world2vec: Mechanistic world models through latent dynamics learning",
  Helmholtz Munich / Munich Center for Machine Learning (MCML),
  arXiv:2610.40637 (October 2026)
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.40637
  https://arxiv.org/html/2610.40637v1
  https://worldmodels.science/
  https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.40637

Found via a bookmarked X post by @shumpeiMaxwell (Shumpei Takezaki):
  https://x.com/shumpeiMaxwell/status/2116343144732377139

Paper verified on arXiv (abs + HTML) and the project page on 2026-11-03.
Official repository (https://github.com/dynamical-inference/world2vec)
exists but states code "will be released soon" — **not vendored**. This
app is an **independent clean-room toy** of continuous-time latent
dynamics matching from pixels + actions with no reward and no pixel
reconstruction — NOT a reproduction of the paper's MuJoCo Pendulum /
Reacher / CartPole tables, DreamerV3 / TD-MPC2 / LeWM comparisons, or
71-attractor system-identification benchmark.

No warranty. Research / demo use. Trained weights stay out of git (work/
is git-ignored).
